{
    "background_story": "Isabella was a 1920s flapper with a flair for the dramatic. Her signature accessory was a worn, crimson fedora, which she'd don at a rakish angle to complete her sultry look. By day, she'd wear it to hide her curly brown locks while she worked as a journalist, sneaking into speakeasies to gather scoops on the city's underground jazz scene. By night, she'd wear it to make a statement, dancing the Charleston with abandon and sipping bootlegged cocktails with the city's elite. Isabella's fedora became a symbol of her independence and free spirit, earning her the nickname 'The Red Hat' among the city's fashionable set. As she navigated the vibrant, tumultuous world of Prohibition-era America, Isabella's trusty fedora remained her constant companion, a reminder of her fearless and adventurous heart.",
